The merge-status card now has an explanatory tooltip, a visible scope label (`Current backlog`), and clickable counts that open the deploy queue filtered by merge state. I also wired the deploy-requests page to honor a `mergeStatus` query param so those links land on a filtered view. I checked the data model before relabeling: this card is backed by `mergeStatus: 'merge_failed'`, not TTL expiry, so I kept `failed` and clarified in the tooltip that expired requests are a separate queue status.

Verification: `npm run lint -- --file src/app/pp/page.tsx --file src/app/pp/deploy-requests/page.tsx` passed. `npx tsc --noEmit` still fails, but only because the repo already has many unrelated pre-existing TypeScript errors outside these files; it did expose and I fixed one local impossible-branch issue in the deploy-requests page.

